message: "If you use this software, please cite the archived release and the associated manuscript."
title: "Boundary crossings as a minimal mechanism for global connectivity in structured landscapes"
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Nelli"
    given-names: "Fabio"

version: "1.1.1"
date-released: 2026-11-01

doi: "10.5281/zenodo.20144948"
repository-code: "https://github.com/meccanismocomplesso/boundary-connectivity-abm"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20144948"
license: MIT

abstract: >-
  Python implementation and reproducibility workflow for an agent-based
  model of boundary-mediated global connectivity in fixed structured
  multi-attractor landscapes. The release contains the core simulation,
  main experimental pipeline, robustness analyses, population-scaling
  analyses, transition-network diagnostics and figure-generation scripts
  associated with the revised manuscript and supplementary material.

keywords:
  - agent-based modeling
  - complex systems
  - network connectivity
  - attractor landscapes
  - boundary crossings
  - heterogeneous mobility
  - stochastic dynamics
  - robustness analysis
  - computational social science
